  "scope": "Actual recovery after callback and actual worker event handler; headless timer/value stubs. Both variants call the same current SessionRecovery in fresh temporary directories. Timing starts at callback invocation, excludes the configured 40 ms timer delay, and delivers the actual completed worker event immediately without Tk polling delay. The benchmark waits for the worker only to measure completion, never as UI guidance. UI dispatch includes the private source copy; final rename and metadata/fsync remain UI work. PNG verification, image decoding, source generation and final directory deletion are untimed. The same lightweight save/copy observers and no-op diagnostic logger are used for both variants.",
  "memory_scope": "Additional owned RGBA source payload only: width*height*4 bytes, one snapshot per candidate trial and no concurrent trial. Excludes the shared borrowed source, Python/native allocator overhead, encoder/hash buffers and all other temporary objects. Process RSS is not measured. Repeated-request coalescing and cancellation are separately covered by lifecycle regressions.",
